"subs": [
{
"t": 3.7,
"dur": 2.511,
"text": "I… I'm still alive. Why are you checking me in?"
},
{
"t": 6.36,
"dur": 3.537,
"text": "The underworld goes by paperwork. Your name's on it. Present."
},
{
"t": 10.297,
"dur": 5.072,
"text": "Hold on. Underworld clerk clocks in on time to check in a very alive company boss."
},
{
"t": 15.619,
"dur": 2.433,
"text": "A mistake? A real one. But the right guy."
},
{
"t": 18.303,
"dur": 1.929,
"text": "Ten days earlier. Here's the story."
},
{
"t": 20.732,
"dur": 5.549,
"text": "I'm a than trung — a death clerk who returns for family. I don't take souls. I keep records."
},
{
"t": 26.53,
"dur": 5.466,
"text": "Case file. Phat Dat Garment Factory. Three hundred workers. Night shift till two a.m."
},
{
"t": 32.246,
"dur": 3.032,
"text": "Director Phat. His catchphrase: “The factory is home.”"
},
{
"t": 35.529,
"dur": 5.304,
"text": "And who clocks out at home? So this time clock only has a clock-in button. No clock-out."
},
{
"t": 41.083,
"dur": 3.853,
"text": "Overtime is dedication! Leave early, lose your attendance bonus!"
},
{
"t": 45.337,
"dur": 5.958,
"text": "Tran Van Loc. Sewing team three. Thursday, two ten a.m. He slumped over his sewing machine."
},
{
"t": 51.544,
"dur": 3.612,
"text": "He didn't get back up. The log says: two ten. At the factory."
},
{
"t": 55.758,
"dur": 1.92,
"text": "Mr. Loc… Mr. Loc."
},
{
"t": 58.178,
"dur": 5.62,
"text": "The first thing the boss asked wasn't how Loc was doing. He asked if the camera covered that spot."
},
{
"t": 64.047,
"dur": 8.681,
"text": "Die at work, on the clock, and it's a workplace accident. They have to pay. Inspectors would ask why the time clock has no clock-out button."
},
{
"t": 72.979,
"dur": 8.057,
"text": "So that night, the boss filled out the report himself. Changed two ten to five a.m. Changed “at the factory” to “at home.”"
},
{
"t": 81.286,
"dur": 7.168,
"text": "Loc's wife hadn't made it up from the countryside. The boss signed as the reporter, too. Relationship: “like family.”"
},
{
"t": 88.704,
"dur": 3.071,
"text": "Team lead Hong stood behind the door. Saw everything."
},
{
"t": 92.025,
"dur": 1.833,
"text": "Whatever the paper says, that's the truth."
},
{
"t": 94.458,
"dur": 4.577,
"text": "I don't read clocks. I read paper. Paper is procedure. Procedure is me."
},
{
"t": 99.285,
"dur": 5.759,
"text": "Five a.m. is a cursed hour. Die then, and I must return to check in one more family member."
},
{
"t": 105.294,
"dur": 2.409,
"text": "Loc's family: one wife. Back home."
},
{
"t": 108.702,
"dur": 3.946,
"text": "Wait. The boss changes the paperwork, and that guy's family pays?"
},
{
"t": 113.048,
"dur": 4.899,
"text": "The rumor raced through the factory faster than a sewing needle. A cursed family death."
},
{
"t": 118.197,
"dur": 4.087,
"text": "Mr. Loc died here at two ten. Everyone on team three knows it."
},
{
"t": 122.535,
"dur": 4.619,
"text": "That cursed death stuff is superstition! Take time off for ghosts, lose your pay!"
},
{
"t": 127.404,
"dur": 5.545,
"text": "The fortune teller at the end of the street is selling cursed-death bracelets, half off. Same guy."
},
{
"t": 133.449,
"dur": 6.163,
"text": "Saturday, three a.m. At the factory. I strike the wooden bell three times and open the case file."
},
{
"t": 139.863,
"dur": 4.86,
"text": "One family member to check in. The report says: Nguyen Van Phat. “Like family.”"
},
{
"t": 144.972,
"dur": 1.984,
"text": "I check in the family member."
},
{
"t": 148.707,
"dur": 2.6,
"text": "At that exact second, the boss's phone lit up."
},
{
"t": 153.107,
"dur": 1.584,
"text": "I'm the boss! I'm not his family!"
},
{
"t": 154.941,
"dur": 2.884,
"text": "You signed the paper. Whatever it says, that's the truth."
},
{
"t": 158.426,
"dur": 5.749,
"text": "There. A mistake. But by the book. Thanks to that mistake, Loc's wife back home sleeps soundly."
},
{
"t": 164.674,
"dur": 1.643,
"text": "Spare me! I'll burn a car for you!"
},
{
"t": 166.568,
"dur": 4.154,
"text": "I ride my bike to work. Your time isn't up. I'm not taking your life."
},
{
"t": 170.973,
"dur": 1.663,
"text": "I'll take your schedule."
},
{
"t": 173.136,
"dur": 7.169,
"text": "Family has to mourn. Every night at three a.m., wrap on a mourning scarf and kneel before Loc's picture. Like his son."
},
{
"t": 180.554,
"dur": 3.454,
"text": "Meet clients during the day. Can't take off the mourning scarf."
},
{
"t": 184.259,
"dur": 6.758,
"text": "Whenever he sleeps through it, the time clock prints his name by itself. By morning, the factory doors are covered in it."
},
{
"t": 191.266,
"dur": 0.984,
"text": "When does this end?"
},
{
"t": 192.65,
"dur": 6.899,
"text": "When the paperwork is right. If it's still wrong after forty-nine days, I'll check you in again. That time, no badge needed."
},
{
"t": 200.548,
"dur": 8.643,
"text": "On night forty-eight, he corrected the report himself. Two ten. At the factory. Workplace accident. Compensation reached Loc's wife."
},
{
"t": 209.441,
"dur": 5.78,
"text": "Two ten isn't a cursed hour. No family member remains on the file. My authority ends here."
},
{
"t": 215.471,
"dur": 3.942,
"text": "Now the time clock has a clock-out button. Overtime gets paid."
},
{
"t": 219.663,
"dur": 5.696,
"text": "I close the file. I didn't take his life. I took his schedule. For a man like this, that hurts more."
},
{
"t": 225.609,
"dur": 4.114,
"text": "Oh. He knelt late three nights. Dock his attendance bonus this month."
},
{
"t": 230.323,
"dur": 7.623,
"text": "Three hundred years perched on cabinets, and this is the first time I've seen the underworld run on time better than a company."
},
{
"t": 238.445,
"dur": 7.42,
"text": "Next time: a child guarding three generations of treasure in an old town house, and the jar no one's allowed to open."
},
{
"t": 246.116,
"dur": 4.909,
"text": "Hit subscribe. Or at three a.m. tonight, your home time clock will print your name."
}
],
